{"skill":{"slug":"deep-research-pro","displayName":"Deep Research Pro"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1770303332827,"changelog":"Re-publish to fix visibility","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":2617,"sha256":"5cfccbf491b066136f0d21abf52eb1bc2711a8166cd0989d840b7f768495b2cc","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4419,"sha256":"a780f8bbec4421982c8276c460f95d1ad82a065182409a730ba952b2dca20015","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"package.json","size":395,"sha256":"7fa0a4ea9ec446b57d55546f44c46181bc016b0edcf878a786d782900bb844d2","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2333,"sha256":"f1aa52c261d29b4008446a95e1ccdd718d4127f851b1739785b9f74c94e90f4b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789035119492,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4df0d608515945ae9a80a9182e317e99ca1a65090b8b64c5ea74fc9e48e95a2c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4df0d608515945ae9a80a9182e317e99ca1a65090b8b64c5ea74fc9e48e95a2c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\n\nThe skill is designed for multi-source deep research, which inherently involves fetching web content. The `SKILL.md` instructs the agent to use `curl -sL \"<url>\"` to retrieve web pages and a Python one-liner to process them, which is a necessary and standard operation for its stated purpose. File writing is confined to `~/clawd/research/` for saving reports. The prompt instructions for sub-agent usage are self-referential, aiming to keep the agent on task rather than subverting its behavior. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection designed to compromise the agent or system.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161588413},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":58,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789035119492},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This research skill fits its stated purpose, but its documented URL-fetching command can let a malicious link run local shell commands and its browsing, saving, and sub-agent behavior is not tightly scoped.","dimensions":[{"detail":"External web/news searches and full-page fetches are purpose-aligned, but arbitrary URL fetching through a shell command is overbroad for safe research and can reach unintended network destinations.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact contains only markdown and package metadata with no install hook or bundled executable, but the README/package mention a scripts/research CLI that is not present in the inspected artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill activates for research on any topic and can browse externally, deep-read URLs, save reports, and optionally run via sub-agent without clear trigger boundaries or consent gates for sensitive topics.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Saving reports under ~/clawd/research is disclosed and purpose-aligned, and there is no system-level persistence, but the skill does not ask before retaining potentially sensitive research prompts or findings.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The web search, page fetching, synthesis, citation, and report saving workflow is coherent for deep research, but the curl template interpolates an untrusted URL into a shell command and does not constrain schemes, hosts, redirects, size, or timeouts.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use this only for non-sensitive research unless you are comfortable with queries, URLs, and reports being processed and stored locally. Do not let it fetch arbitrary or untrusted URLs through the documented shell template; a safer implementation should validate URLs and call curl without shell interpolation.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Accepted in substance: the SKILL.md command `curl -sL \"<url>\" | python3 -c ...` can evaluate shell substitutions embedded in a search- or user-derived URL before curl runs.\n[SC2] expected: External page fetching is expected for deep research, but the artifact lacks URL validation, protocol restrictions, redirect controls, and size/time limits, so the implementation guidance is under-scoped.\n[SQP-1] expected: A broad research trigger is normal for this skill type, but combining it with external browsing, local report writes, and optional sub-agent use creates a real consent and scoping concern.\n[SQP-2] expected: Saving reports locally is part of the stated feature set, but the artifact does not provide a no-save default, overwrite guidance, or warnings for confidential research topics.\n[AS3] expected: Downgraded: the cited sub-agent example tells a spawned agent to read this skill's own installed SKILL.md, not to enumerate or read unrelated peer skills.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789035119492}}}}}